<section class="band">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="band-head"><h2>The thirtieth conference</h2><a class="textlink" href="/conferences/">Full review →</a></div>
    <div class="review">
      <figure><img src="/images/olxxx-hero-panel.jpg" alt="Catholic and Orthodox hierarchs on the panel at Orientale Lumen XXX" width="1200" height="900"><figcaption>Cardinal Seán O'Malley, Metropolitan Tikhon, Archbishop Flavio Pace, and bishops of the Greek Orthodox, Romanian Catholic, and Roman Catholic Churches, moderated by Dr. John Borelli of Georgetown. St. John Paul II Shrine, July 13 to 15, 2026.</figcaption></figure>
      <div>
        <p class="lede">Orientale Lumen XXX closed on the eve of July 16, the anniversary of the schism of 1054, with one question on the table: consensus achieved, what's next?</p>
        <p>Two moments will be remembered. Archbishop Gabriele Caccia, the Apostolic Nuncio, presented Jack Figel with the official medal of Pope Leo XIV's first year, sent by the Holy Father. And on the final day Cardinal Kurt Koch, Prefect of the Dicastery for Promoting Christian Unity, addressed the conference by video from Rome: the progress of the dialogue, he said, must not remain the property of experts.</p>
        <p>EWTN News covered the conference nationally. <a class="textlink" href="/conferences/">Read the review and watch the Cardinal's address →</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

